# A spatial family of the original source

Open boxes reuse the native occupation code, complete Gauss references
and original Wilson rule. Recorded code admissions assemble a known
nonstationary state with vanishing failure probability. A uniform graph
propagation bound and finite photon budgets apply at every box size.
Complete local electric and magnetic observer histories have a
controlled volume limit at fixed spacing, including bounded positive
autonomous times under the coupled source. The
[dynamic proof](DYNAMICS.md) retains the full field/Coulomb baseline
and controls the removed distant bounded hopping terms.

The [proof](PROOF.md) also derives the original regulator's exact
matter/photon squared-dispersion mismatch. Increasing volume does not
remove it. No larger-volume interacting ground, zero-spacing limit or
Lorentz covariance is asserted. Every finite member retains all banks,
preparation flags and Gauss references; the limit concerns the fixed
observer's complete local record marginal.

Run `python -B producer.py --check` and `python -m pytest -q .` with
the repository environment. All large photon budgets are analytic;
their full native matrices are not numerically enumerated.
